  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Find the integer values of $a$ and $b$ in each of the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$3+4\\sqrt5=a+2\\sqrt b$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=3,\\ b=20$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3+4\\sqrt5&=3+2(2\\sqrt5)\\\\3+4\\sqrt5&=3+2\\sqrt{20}\\end{align*}$$\nThe rational term is $3$. For integer $b$ giving an irrational root, $\\sqrt b$ has no rational term, so $a=3$ and $b=20$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(2-3\\sqrt5)^2=a+b\\sqrt5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=49,\\ b=-12$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2-3\\sqrt5)^2&=4-12\\sqrt5+45\\\\(2-3\\sqrt5)^2&=49-12\\sqrt5\\end{align*}$$\nMatch the rational term and the coefficient of $\\sqrt5$ to get $a=49$ and $b=-12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(2\\sqrt3-3\\sqrt6)^2=a+b\\sqrt2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=66,\\ b=-36$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2\\sqrt3-3\\sqrt6)^2&=12-12\\sqrt{18}+54\\\\(2\\sqrt3-3\\sqrt6)^2&=12-36\\sqrt2+54\\\\(2\\sqrt3-3\\sqrt6)^2&=66-36\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\nMatch the rational term and the coefficient of $\\sqrt2$ to get $a=66$ and $b=-36$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(1-3\\sqrt2)^2-(2+3\\sqrt2)^2=a+b\\sqrt2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-3,\\ b=-18$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1-3\\sqrt2)^2&=1-6\\sqrt2+18\\\\(1-3\\sqrt2)^2&=19-6\\sqrt2\\\\(2+3\\sqrt2)^2&=4+12\\sqrt2+18\\\\(2+3\\sqrt2)^2&=22+12\\sqrt2\\\\(1-3\\sqrt2)^2-(2+3\\sqrt2)^2&=(19-6\\sqrt2)-(22+12\\sqrt2)\\\\(1-3\\sqrt2)^2-(2+3\\sqrt2)^2&=-3-18\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\nMatch the rational term and the coefficient of $\\sqrt2$ to get $a=-3$ and $b=-18$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
